Development Milestones
This public changelog documents selected, non-sensitive milestones of AIAQ Knowledge Intelligence System (KIS) 1.0.

The implementation is maintained privately within AIAQ Lab's AI Hub. Development history, source documents, raw test evidence, internal configuration, prompts, credentials, and proprietary engineering details are intentionally excluded.
Milestones below distinguish completed local validation from planned or partially validated functionality. They do not imply unrestricted production authorization.

November 2026 — Foundation and Local MVP
Milestone 1 — Knowledge Intelligence Strategy
- Defined KIS as a local-first retrieval and project-context layer over existing AI Hub services.
- Identified three core use cases: source-grounded search, project re-entry, and evidence-assisted engineering review.
- Established the principle that original project materials remain authoritative and the index is only a derived retrieval layer.
- Excluded unnecessary new services and uncontrolled cloud dependencies from the initial scope.
Outcome: a bounded architecture and an evidence-first development path.
Milestone 2 — Retrieval Backend Validation
- Evaluated the available self-hosted retrieval infrastructure.
- Selected reuse of the existing Open WebUI / Chroma environment rather than deploying a duplicate vector database.
- Validated the local retrieval foundation and supported service boundaries in controlled checks.
Outcome: an established backend direction for the limited local MVP.
Milestone 3 — Controlled Knowledge Ingestion
- Introduced a limited approved-source corpus for the first retrieval experiments.
- Recorded a pilot baseline of 6 documents / 165 chunks, including 4 pilot documents.
- Exercised indexing and controlled backup/restore checks.
- Kept original project materials outside the public repository.
Outcome: a reproducible small-corpus foundation for further retrieval testing.
Milestone 4 — Hybrid Search and Scoped Retrieval
- Developed the exact-match and semantic-search workflow for complementary query types.
- Added scoped retrieval and result-combination logic.
- Exercised live retrieval against the limited local environment.
- Continued work on relevance and trustworthy freshness indicators rather than assuming that indexed content is always current.
Outcome: scoped live retrieval verified; quality and freshness hardening remain active.
Milestone 5 — Project Re-entry and Evidence Review
- Introduced project-context recovery as a separate workflow from ordinary search.
- Added an advisory evidence-review path designed to expose gaps and uncertain states.
- Preserved explicit partial/review outcomes instead of reporting unsupported completion.
Outcome: project re-entry is PARTIAL; evidence-assisted review remains REVIEW_REQUIRED where proof is insufficient.
Milestone 6 — Regression and User-Scenario Validation
- Expanded the regression suite across the bounded local MVP.
- Recorded 145 / 145 automated checks passed in the latest available internal baseline.
- Accepted 3 / 3 primary user scenarios for the limited local scope.
- Confirmed scoped live retrieval without treating it as proof of every production dependency.
Outcome: a validated local MVP baseline, with results limited to the tested candidate and environment.
Milestone 7 — Controlled Owner Admission
- Established a limited owner-approved operating scope for the local CLI workflow.
- Kept production modification and release authority outside the retrieval and AI-review components.
- Recorded unresolved boundaries explicitly, including server-index as-of state, re-entry completeness, evidence-review limitations, and sustained stability.
Outcome: limited local Owner GO; full Production GO not yet established.
Current Engineering Priorities
The next improvements are driven by actual validation gaps:
- Make source freshness and index state independently verifiable.
- Improve relevance on representative project questions and negative cases.
- Complete more reliable project re-entry context packs.
- Strengthen evidence linkage without granting an AI reviewer release authority.
- Confirm runtime recovery, stability, and the remaining production admission checks.
- Expand the source corpus only when permissions and practical value justify it.
No external cloud access, extra vector infrastructure, unrestricted autonomous operation, or customer-data ingestion is implied by this roadmap.
Current Status
As of November 19, 2026: internal operational MVP with limited local owner approval; full production authorization remains unconfirmed.

The project will continue to publish selected, sanitized milestones while the engineering implementation stays private.
